  "verbalization": "Digitoxigenin appears to exert its biological effects through a shared pathway involving SK-HEP1 cells, which are targeted by both Digitoxigenin and other compounds such as Massarinin B. This suggests that Digitoxigenin may act on SK-HEP1 cells through a mechanism that is conserved across different compounds. The evidence indicates that SK-HEP1 cells are targets of multiple compounds, and each of these compounds ultimately leads to the activation of the CD276 antigen. This suggests that the CD276 antigen may be a downstream effector of the signaling pathways activated by these compounds. The presence of a direct link from the compound to the CD276 antigen, along with the involvement of SK-HEP1 cells as intermediaries, supports the hypothesis that Digitoxigenin may interact with CD276 antigen through a mechanism that involves SK-HEP1 cells. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Digitoxigenin to influence CD276 antigen expression via a complex network of molecular interactions.",
